========================================================================================
                               COMMAND FLOW EXPLANATIONS
========================================================================================

1. docker run (Solid Line ──>)
   Client  --> Sends execution command to Docker daemon.
   Daemon  --> Checks local Images cache.
   Host    --> Spins up and runs live, isolated Containers.

2. docker build (Dotted Line ···>)
   Client  --> Sends your local "recipe" (Dockerfile) to the Docker daemon.
   Daemon  --> Bakes the recipe and stores a brand new blueprint in local Images.

3. docker pull (Dashed Line - - >)
   Client  --> Requests a specific pre-made image from the daemon.
   Daemon  --> Reaches out to the online Registry (Docker Hub) to download it.
   Host    --> Saves the downloaded file into local Images for later use.

docker daemon - manages all the components of docker in container & images
image - read only templates from which containers are created. a continer always created from image

